# Keep CLAUDE.md out of what a student unpacks.
#
# This repo IS the ~/cs193v layout — the installer downloads
# https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>/archive/refs/heads/<branch>.tar.gz and unpacks it into
# the student's course directory. That directory is deliberately kept to TWO visible items,
# the launcher and projects/ (issue #16), so a developer-facing CLAUDE.md sitting next to
# them would undo that.
#
# GitHub builds those archives with `git archive`, which honours export-ignore, so the file
# is present for anyone working in the repo and absent from every student download.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Patterns here match like .gitignore ones: without it,
# `CLAUDE.md` matches that basename at ANY depth, which also strips
# files/claude-code/CLAUDE.md -- the managed Claude Code policy the image installs into
# /etc/claude-code. Verified: unanchored, that file was in the tree and absent from the
# archive, so building the image from a downloaded tarball would have failed. Anchored, only
# the root file goes.
#
# Verify both halves after changing this:
#
#     git archive HEAD | tar -t | grep -c '^CLAUDE.md'                # expect 0
#     git archive HEAD | tar -t | grep -c 'claude-code/CLAUDE.md'     # expect 1
#
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore

# CRLF ON THE BATCH FILE IS LOAD-BEARING, and this is the only thing that keeps it.
#
# cmd.exe does not read a batch file line by line. It reads it in 512-BYTE CHUNKS, and its label
# scanner assumes a two-byte \r\n terminator. Under LF-only endings that scanner drifts, so
# `goto` and `call :label` fail depending on the BYTE OFFSET of the label -- inserting or deleting
# a byte anywhere earlier in the file makes the bug appear or vanish, and duplicating labels does
# not fix it. install-cs193v-windows.cmd is entirely `goto`-structured, so it is maximally
# exposed. It shipped LF-only until this rule existed.
#
# `text eol=crlf` and not `-text`: both produce CRLF today, but this one is self-healing. The repo
# stores LF, and checkout AND `git archive` both convert -- so a TA who commits from an editor
# that saved LF still ships a working file, where `-text` would preserve the mistake verbatim.
#
# Wine CANNOT catch a regression here: its cmd reads bare \n natively (batch.c:259-266), so the
# --tier windows run passes either way. 25-installer.sh asserts it statically instead.
#
# Verify after changing this -- the archive is what a student actually downloads:
#
#     git archive HEAD .private/install-cs193v-windows.cmd | tar -xO | file -
#         # expect: ... with CRLF line terminators
#
*.cmd text eol=crlf
